::ENG2_U04_L03_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.RS.01] Research question: How could a school garden support science learning? Source A says gardens let students observe plant growth, soil conditions, and ecosystem relationships. Which note is most useful?{
~A. Gardens are outside.#Incorrect. This is true but too general to answer the research question.
=B. Gardens can support observations of plant growth, soil, and ecosystems.#Correct. This note is brief, accurate, and relevant to the research question.
~C. Students are people.#Incorrect. This does not help answer the research question.
~D. The source has words.#Incorrect. This is not useful source information.
}

::ENG2_U04_L03_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Original: Garden journals can help students record observations and connect evidence to science vocabulary. Which paraphrase is accurate?{
~A. Journals make science unnecessary.#Incorrect. The original says journals support science work.
~B. Garden journals are always perfect.#Incorrect. The original does not make that absolute claim.
~C. Students should never write observations.#Incorrect. The original says journals help students record observations.
=D. Students can use garden journals to track what they see and explain it with science terms.#Correct. This keeps the meaning in new wording.
}

::ENG2_U04_L03_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.RS.01] Source A says gardens provide real plant observations. Source B says journals help students compare observations over time. Which synthesis is strongest?{
=A. Gardens give students observations, and journals help students track and compare those observations over time.#Correct. This combines the two sources into one connected explanation.
~B. Source A is about gardens. Source B is about journals.#Incorrect. This lists sources but does not connect them.
~C. Gardens and journals are words.#Incorrect. This is not synthesis.
~D. Science learning is impossible.#Incorrect. This contradicts the source information.
}

::ENG2_U04_L03_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.RS.01] Source C says a pre-order lunch pilot reduced unwanted trays but students needed reminders during the first week. Which paraphrase keeps the full meaning?{
~A. The pre-order form solved every problem perfectly.#Incorrect. This leaves out the reminder challenge.
~B. The pre-order form did nothing at all.#Incorrect. This ignores the reduction in unwanted trays.
=C. The pre-order pilot reduced unwanted trays, but students needed reminders at first.#Correct. This includes both the benefit and the limitation.
~D. Students never forgot the form.#Incorrect. The source says reminders were needed.
}

::ENG2_U04_L03_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence uses clear standard English for a synthesis statement?{
~A. Garden good journals stuff because science.#Incorrect. This is not standard English.
=B. A school garden can support science learning when students observe plant growth and use journals to record evidence.#Correct. This sentence is clear, complete, and evidence-based.
~C. Journals, garden, science, because.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~D. They do it and that thing is there.#Incorrect. This is vague and unclear.
}
